{
  "_help": [
    "Third-party AI provider approvals. Framework and process: docs/third-party-ai/README.md.",
    "One entry per outside service SSAI can send data to: every non-local provider in ai_models.json, plus integrations (Microsoft Copilot).",
    "status: approved | pending | rejected. 'approved' needs every checklist item true, 'reviewed' (date) and 'reviewer'; backend/tools/test_provider_approvals.py enforces it.",
    "A checklist item is true only once the provider has confirmed it IN WRITING (contract, DPA, published terms you have saved a copy of) and the evidence is listed in the provider's record.",
    "Enforcement is opt-in: SSAI_REQUIRE_PROVIDER_APPROVAL=1 in .env keeps every cloud provider that is not 'approved' out of the AI panel. Turn it on for customer deployments.",
    "This installation's own decisions go in instance/provider_approvals.json (same shape, only the entries you change; it survives updates).",
    "Local models (Ollama on this network) never leave the network and need no entry; an Ollama endpoint on the internet is treated as cloud and is not covered by the 'ollama' entry."
  ],
